      "message": "`build_allocations` has no overlap test: it takes `min(start)` and `max(end)` over every schedule sharing an `assignment_id` (src/quads/tools/allocation_graph.py:151-152), then clips to the window. An assignment with host A on Jun 1-5 and host B on Jul 20-25 becomes one block covering Jun 1 to Jul 25, so the gap reads as occupied and the tooltip shows only the merged bounds. `POST /schedules` can attach a caller-dated schedule to an existing assignment, so disjoint windows are reachable. Either say \"merges all schedules for the same assignment\" or group by overlapping interval. Non-blocking: docs/quads-workflow.md does not repeat this claim.",
      "revId": "a04b95c36a24c0500ead59102431ee1a50724edb",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
