      "side": 1,
      "message": "No scaling relative to the largest block exists. `_render_block` computes `max(MIN_MACHINE_HEIGHT_PX, min(MAX_BLOCK_HEIGHT_PX, host_count * MAX_MACHINE_HEIGHT_PX))` (src/quads/tools/allocation_graph.py:241-244): a fixed 18px step per machine, clamped at both ends. A 4-host block is 72px whatever its peers are, and 20 and 40 hosts both render 360px. Say \"proportional to machine count, capped at MAX_BLOCK_HEIGHT_PX\" so the spec matches the renderer.",
